{"summary":"The red-billed quelea (Quelea quelea), also known as the red-billed weaver or red-billed dioch, is a small—approximately 12 cm (4.7 in) long and weighing 15–26 g (0.53–0.92 oz)—migratory, sparrow-like bird of the weaver family, Ploceidae, native to Sub-Saharan Africa. It was named by Linnaeus in 1758, who considered it a bunting, but Ludwig Reichenbach assigned it in 1850 to the new genus Quelea. Three subspecies are recognised, with Quelea quelea quelea occurring roughly from Senegal to Chad, Q. q. aethiopica from Sudan...","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quelea quelea","cells":[[-21.6,22.1,1],[-17.6,20.0,1],[-19.0,18.6,2],[-20.3,22.1,1],[-19.0,13.7,1],[-16.3,14.4,1],[-20.3,15.8,1],[-19.0,17.9,1],[-20.3,14.4,1],[-21.6,16.5,1],[-18.3,22.1,1],[-19.6,18.6,1],[-19.0,15.1,1],[-17.6,14.4,1],[-19.0,14.4,1],[-21.6,21.4,1],[-19.0,20.7,1],[-19.6,15.1,2],[-19.6,17.9,1],[-20.3,17.2,2],[-19.6,17.2,1],[-20.3,16.5,1],[-21.0,16.5,2],[-19.6,20.7,1],[-19.0,17.2,2],[-17.6,13.7,2],[-18.3,17.2,1],[-18.3,16.5,1],[-21.6,15.8,1],[-17.0,13.0,1],[-20.3,15.1,1],[-19.0,16.5,2],[-21.0,15.1,1],[-18.3,21.4,2],[-19.6,15.8,2],[-19.6,14.4,2],[-19.0,15.8,2],[-15.6,30.6,1],[-20.3,22.9,1],[-21.0,27.8,1],[-15.6,25.7,1],[-20.3,23.6,1],[-17.0,34.8,1],[-17.0,23.6,1],[-19.0,25.0,1],[-19.6,25.0,1],[-21.6,32.0,1],[-15.6,29.9,1],[-16.3,28.5,1],[-19.0,27.1,1],[-18.3,26.4,1],[-20.3,25.0,1],[-17.6,24.3,1],[-17.0,25.0,1],[-15.6,27.8,1],[-20.3,24.3,1],[-18.3,25.7,2],[-17.0,26.4,1],[-16.3,29.9,1],[-17.6,30.6,1],[-16.3,34.8,2],[-21.0,24.3,1],[-21.6,29.9,1],[-17.6,31.3,2],[-21.0,23.6,1],[-16.3,27.8,1],[-15.6,27.1,1],[-21.0,32.0,2],[-15.6,28.5,2],[-21.0,22.9,1],[-19.6,26.4,2],[-21.0,30.6,1],[-20.3,32.0,2],[-21.0,31.3,1],[-20.3,26.4,1],[-21.6,23.6,2],[-19.0,24.3,2],[-19.6,32.7,1],[-19.6,23.6,2],[-21.0,29.2,1],[-19.6,29.9,1],[-17.0,28.5,1],[-15.6,34.8,2],[-19.6,22.9,2],[-19.0,22.9,2],[-17.6,26.4,2],[-19.0,26.4,1],[-19.0,23.6,2],[-19.0,34.1,2],[-20.3,28.5,2],[-21.0,32.7,1],[-17.0,27.8,1],[-16.3,29.2,2],